**Extract:**

Figure 2 shows the oxygen dissociation curve for haemoglobin.

Fig. 2 shows the following about the relationship between pO~2~ and the affinity of haemoglobin for oxygen...

- At low pO~2~ the affinity of haemoglobin for oxygen is low;
- Haemoglobin binds slowly to oxygen at low pO~2~ / oxygen saturation is low at low pO~2~;
- At high pO~2~ the affinity of haemoglobin for oxygen is high;
- Saturation of haemoglobin with oxygen is high at high pO~2~;

Anaemia is a condition in which an individual's blood contains less haemoglobin than usual. Individuals with anaemia can produce chemicals in their blood which influence the haemoglobin dissociation curve, as shown in Figure 3.

